abstract: >-
  Supporting experiments for a research perspective on evidence sufficiency
  in AI investigation, with a proposed collaborative research agenda.
  A controlled cloud-log study compares original and clarified
  instructions and inspects unsupported assertions about withheld fields.
  The companion contains 996 categorical decision records and 306 exact
  Splunk-based input/output replays from two local models, and an exploratory
  November run of Claude Sonnet 5.5 through Claude Code (480 calls) with its
  preregistration, per-history counts and 24 exact Splunk-based responses.
  It supports retained-response analysis, not a claim of fresh inference
  replication or operational defense efficacy.
  License identifiers apply to different components as mapped in LICENSING.md.
